  "precedence": [
    "0. OEM protective-stop/interlock status: TERMINATE OEM_STOP_ACTIVE (independent external authority; not a Haplous safety function).",
    "1. Authority and lifecycle: active revocation/lease expiration TERMINATE; invalid owner/resource/epoch/ACK REFUSE; authority wins over capability/time.",
    "2. Capabilities and admission: required control behavior, sensor, calibration and verified+authorized substitutions. Never silently downgrade.",
    "3. Clock-domain validity and bounded future-skew: invalid mapped clock/refusal before age-based checks.",
    "4. Command deadline: expired command REFUSE.",
    "5. Observation validity: stale SUSPEND, including selected-mode-specific freshness requirement.",
    "6. Execution mode handover: pending/unconfirmed mode switch SUSPEND.",
    "7. Otherwise ADMIT; report actual selected mode and verified substitution if applicable."
  ],
  "mode_semantics": "Mode equality is allowed; a behavioral alternative requires BOTH explicit contract authorization and independently verified machine equivalence for the same required behavior. joint_torque (literal low-level torque authority) is NOT equivalent to native_force merely by policy preference. Positive example is behavior bounded_cartesian_compliance -> verified native_force.",
  "baseline_profile": "baseline_g0_minimal_guards (non-competitive component ablation; timeout/mode availability/external stop only). See BASELINE_SPEC.md."
